Function ArrayOfChar.Clear(VAR str : ARRAY OF CHAR) | Set length of string to 0
Function ArrayOfChar.NulTerminate(VAR str : ARRAY OF CHAR) | Ensure string is `NUL` terminated
Function ArrayOfChar.Length(str: ARRAY OF CHAR) : LENGTH |Find length of C style `NUL` terminated string or length of array if not `NUL` terminated
Function ArrayOfChar.Capacity(str- : ARRAY OF CHAR): LENGTH | Return capacity of the array
Function ArrayOfChar.Assign(VAR dst : ARRAY OF CHAR; src- : ARRAY OF CHAR) | Assign `src` to `dst`
Function ArrayOfChar.FillChar(VAR dst : ARRAY OF CHAR; ch : CHAR) | Fill string `dst` with char `chr`
Function ArrayOfChar.AppendChar(VAR dst : ARRAY OF CHAR; ch : CHAR) | Append `ch` to `dst`
Function ArrayOfChar.Append(VAR dst : ARRAY OF CHAR; src- : ARRAY OF CHAR) | Append `src` to `dst`
Function ArrayOfChar.Extract(VAR dst : ARRAY OF CHAR; src- : ARRAY OF CHAR; start, count: LENGTH) | Extract substring to `dst` from `src` from `start` position and `count` length.
Function ArrayOfChar.Compare(left-, right- : ARRAY OF CHAR): INTEGER | Compare strings `left` and `right`
Function ArrayOfChar.Equal(left-, right- : ARRAY OF CHAR): BOOLEAN | Test if `left` and `right` is equal
Function ArrayOfChar.IndexChar(ch : CHAR; str- : ARRAY OF CHAR; start: LENGTH): LENGTH | Index of `char` in `str`. zero based index with -1 indicating `char` not found
Function ArrayOfChar.Index(pattern-, str-: ARRAY OF CHAR; start : LENGTH): LENGTH | Index of `pattern` in `str`. -1 indicating pattern not found
Function ArrayOfChar.Delete(VAR dst: ARRAY OF CHAR; start, count: LENGTH) | Delete `count` characters from `dst` starting from `start`
Function ArrayOfChar.Insert(VAR dst : ARRAY OF CHAR; src- : ARRAY OF CHAR; start: LENGTH) | Insert `src` into `dst` at `start`
Function ArrayOfChar.Replace(VAR dst: ARRAY OF CHAR; old-, new-: ARRAY OF CHAR; start : LENGTH) | Replace `old` string with `new` string starting at index `start`
Function ArrayOfChar.LeftTrim(VAR dst: ARRAY OF CHAR) | Remove white space & control characters from left side of string
Function ArrayOfChar.RightTrim(VAR dst: ARRAY OF CHAR) | Remove white space & special characters from right side of string
Function ArrayOfChar.LeftPad(VAR dst: ARRAY OF CHAR; width : LENGTH; ch : CHAR) | Left justified of length `width` with `ch`
Function ArrayOfChar.RightPad(VAR dst: ARRAY OF CHAR; width : LENGTH; ch : CHAR) | Right justified of length `width` with `ch`
Function ArrayOfChar.Trim(VAR dst: ARRAY OF CHAR) | Remove white space & special characters from right & left side of string
Function ArrayOfChar.LowerCase(VAR dst: ARRAY OF CHAR) | Transform string inplace to lower case (Only takes into account the ASCII characters)
Function ArrayOfChar.UpperCase(VAR dst: ARRAY OF CHAR) | Transform string inplace to upper case (Only takes into account the ASCII characters)
Function ArrayOfChar.Capitalize(VAR dst: ARRAY OF CHAR) | Capitalize string inplace
Function ArrayOfChar.StartsWith(str-, prefix- : ARRAY OF CHAR): BOOLEAN | Check if string `str` starts with `prefix`
Function ArrayOfChar.EndsWith(str-, postfix- : ARRAY OF CHAR): BOOLEAN | Check if string `str` ends with `postfix`
Function ArrayOfChar.Match(str- : ARRAY OF CHAR; pattern- : ARRAY OF CHAR; IgnoreCase : BOOLEAN): BOOLEAN | Return `TRUE` if `patter` matches `str`
Function ArrayOfChar.Format(VAR Writer : Type.Stream; str- : ARRAY OF CHAR; width, prec: INTEGER; flags: SET) | Format `ARRAY OF CHAR`. 
Function ArrayOfChar.Hash(src- : ARRAY OF CHAR): LENGTH | Hash value of string (64/32bit FNV-1a)
Function Char.IsControl(ch: CHAR) : BOOLEAN | Returns true of ch is a control character
Function Char.IsDigit(ch: CHAR) : BOOLEAN | Returns true of ch is a digit
Function Char.IsLetter(ch: CHAR) : BOOLEAN | Returns true of ch is a letter
Function Char.IsSpace(ch: CHAR) : BOOLEAN | Returns true of ch is a white space character
Function Char.IsLower(ch: CHAR) : BOOLEAN | Returns true of ch is a lower case letter
Function Char.IsUpper(ch: CHAR) : BOOLEAN | Returns true of ch is a upper case letter
Function Char.Lower(ch: CHAR) : CHAR | Returns lower case letter or unmodified char
Function Char.Upper(ch: CHAR) : CHAR | Returns upper case letter or unmodified char
